Model answer:
R = \sqrt{(1)^2 + (1)^2} = \sqrt{2}
R\cos\alpha = 1,\ R\sin\alpha = 1 \Rightarrow \tan\alpha = 1,\ \alpha = \frac{\pi}{4}
\sqrt{2}\sin(x + \alpha) = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \Rightarrow \sin(x + \alpha) = \frac{1}{2}
Solve for x + \alpha in \alpha \le x + \alpha \le 2\pi + \alpha, then subtract \alpha:
x = \frac{7 \pi}{12}, x = \frac{23 \pi}{12}

Marking guideline (4 marks, award the highest band the response fully meets):
- Correct R and α and all solutions (4 marks)
- Correct R and α with some correct solutions (3 marks)
- Correct R and α (2 marks)
- Correct R (1 mark)
Equivalent methods and wording that show the same understanding get the same marks.
